  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> be the point of intersection of the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now let,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p>Say, point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Since point lie on the plane also,</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the point will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now finding the distance of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>144</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>78</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>Equation with roots <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>q</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>72</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
